{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 100)` priors for `sigma_a` and `sigma_y`. These parameters were already constrained to `[0, 100]`, so the added priors make the implicit bounded uniform priors explicit for SafeStan without changing the posterior except for a constant log-density offset. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with the built-in `normal` distribution. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] u;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  real b;
  vector[J] eta;
  real mu_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[J] a;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  a = mu_a + sigma_a * eta;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[county[i]] + u[i] * b * 0.1;
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta ~ normal(0, 1);
  b ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":3,"N":4,"county":[1,1,1,1],"u":[4.40904669920361,5.506291362644063,5.025425829983101,4.5922100430639805],"y":[3.0,4.0,2.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
